(emphasis added) (quoting 22 U.S.C. § 618(f)).           Such texts easily
warrant a subset-superset interpretation. When Congress uses “a list
of specific items separated by commas and followed by a general or
collective term,” it raises the “inference . . . that Congress remained
focused on the common attribute when it used the catchall phrase.”
Ali v. Fed. Bureau of Prisons, 552 U.S. 214, 225 (2008) (discussing the
