      Finally, the government’s interpretation undermines the very
purpose that it purports to advance—treating similarly situated
noncitizens alike.    If the government is correct about Section
1225(b)(2)(A), then an unlawfully present noncitizen who entered
illegally must be detained, but an unlawfully present noncitizen who
