identical in all other respects. Thus, even if both noncitizens had lived
in the country for many years and were enmeshed in their
communities, only the unlawful entrant would need to be detained,
even though both noncitizens violated our immigration laws. At
bottom, an illegal entrant and a visa overstayer who have both lived
in the country for many years are much more similar to each other
than to an unknown noncitizen who has just arrived at the border for
inspection and admission. The government’s interpretation therefore
results in a much more problematic form of unequal treatment than
Petitioner’s does.




