Even when an agency has historically exercised some power pursuant a
statute, its longstanding lack of any prior assertion of the expanded power
that it now seeks to employ under that same statute can still be “significant
in determining whether such power was actually conferred.” Bunte Bros.,
312 U.S. at 352; see id. at 351–52 (holding that, even though the Federal Trade
Commission exercised authority under a statute against business practices
