197-A number of commenters expressed concern with section 240.20(b) of the proposed regulation, which states that an application for cancellation of removal may be filed only with the Immigration Court after jurisdiction has vested pursuant to section 8 CFR 3.14. Section 3.14(a) provides that jurisdiction vests when a charging document is filed with the Immigration Court by the Service. The practical concern raised by the commenters arise if the Service serves Form I–862, Notice to Appear, on a respondent but does not file it with the Immigration Court. If the Service does not file a notice to appear which has been served, a respondent would not have access to the Immigration Court to obtain forms of relief such as cancellation of removal or adjustment of status. Moreover, the service of the notice to appear will cut off the accrual of time in continuous residence or continuous physical presence for that respondent under new section 240A(d)(1) of the Act. The commenters proposed that language be added to § 3.14(a) of the regulation allowing for jurisdiction to vest and
