237-through no fault of his own, has not obtained travel documents. The regulation already provides, at § 240.26(b)(3)(ii), that the Service in its discretion may extend the period within which the alien must provide such documentation. However, the provision for extension is discretionary and not an entitlement. The alien in removal proceedings bears the responsibility to demonstrate eligibility for any relief requested. The alien is encouraged to work with the government of his or her home country to obtain a valid passport or other travel authorization if a travel document is necessary for return to that country. Failure to obtain necessary travel documentation will leave the Department no option but to enforce the alternate order of removal.
