checks/audits/immigration-detention--2026-10-01-supreme-court-takes-up-bond-hearings-2026-10-03-record-audit.log:10930:| **Major, B: hearing versus release** | “an immigration judge released him on bond” | The [Second Circuit opinion](/Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-detention/data/sources/immigration-detention/ca2-cunha-opinion-2026-04-28.txt:155) says the judge found no danger or flight risk. Section [1226(a)](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/USCODE-2024-title8/html/USCODE-2024-title8-chap12-subchapII-partIV-sec1226.htm) says the government **may** release an arrested person on bond. Winning access to a hearing does not itself require release. | Add one sentence explaining the hearing’s decision and the case’s individual stakes. |
